FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] tests/loop_bounds_test.rs:336 — `step_budget_makes_a_runaway_loop_assertable` asserts `Error::Runtime` on `set stopped to 0\nwhile stopped is 0\n    set count to count + 1\nend` where `count` is never declared, so the first iteration fails with unknown-variable `Runtime` and the 200-step budget is never reached — the test passes for the wrong reason and a step-budget regression would stay green — declare `count` before the loop and assert `Error::Limit`.
2. [MAJOR] src/testing/assertions.rs:130 — `assert_text_matches` does `Regex::new(pattern).map(|re| re.is_match(text)).unwrap_or(false)`, conflating an unparseable pattern with a non-match under the identical `does not match pattern` message — caller cannot tell bad pattern from failed match — return a distinct `Err` naming invalid pattern on `Regex::new` failure.
3. [MAJOR] tests/numeric_edge_test.rs:696 — limit-message helpers were widened to `Error::Runtime(message, span) | Error::Limit(message, span)` (same at tests/loop_bounds_test.rs:49, tests/for_range_test.rs:63, tests/loop_control_test.rs:59, tests/object_model_test.rs:81, tests/function_literal_test.rs:79) then only check message text, so a flip back to `Runtime` still passes and `is_resource_limit()` is unpinned — match only `Error::Limit` or assert `error.is_resource_limit()` in limit tests.
4. [MINOR] phases/phase-039/REPORT.md:80 — cites `Error::kind()` at `src/error.rs:92` returning `RuntimeError` for `Error::Limit`, but `src/error.rs:84` defines `label()`, no `kind()` exists — repair justification references a non-existent API — correct citation to `label()`.
